# Non-Nix pins (template authors)

When adding a tool Nix does not package: pin it in one file, add
`includes/update/<name>.sh`, and do not teach consumers to bump the copy.

```
# ❌ BAD — consumers "upgrade" by editing the copied pin
# home/llm-context.nix
serenaVersion = "1.8.0";

# ✅ GOOD — pin here, refresher owns the bump, users get it via copier update
# home/llm-context.nix
serenaVersion = "1.7.0";
# includes/update/pypi-llm.sh  →  replace_nix_string_assign … serenaVersion
```

`update` in this checkout runs those refreshers. It does not run
`devenv update` or `refresh-toolchain-latest`. Copier excludes this rule.
